  "section_notes": "S2 contains no numeric permanent limit: the 5% figure is a corrective-action trigger, and sales are never automatically stopped, which is the main benefit to Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%). S5 keeps a mandatory 8/100k recall trigger with no interim allowance, which exposes Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9/100k), while S4's 36-month suppression deadline and numeric customer results favour Halcyon's red lines. S1 (24-hour reporting covering all incidents) is the strongest section and applies to both companies' unreported incidents."
